# npm vs npx

## npm (Node Package Manager)
Installs packages **permanently** into your project (or globally).
Use when you'll need the package repeatedly across sessions.

```bash
npm install express     # installs and saves to package.json
npm i -g nodemon        # install globally, available anywhere
```

## npx (Node Package eXecute)
Runs a package **once, on the spot**, without permanently installing it.
Use when you only need to run it once (e.g., scaffolding tools).

```bash
npx create-react-app my-app   # runs without installing globally
```

---

**Analogy:**
> Calling a plumber who stays at your house full-time = **npm** (permanent install)
> Calling a plumber only when you need them = **npx** (one-time run)
